  "fluff": {
    "overview": "<p>The Zechetinu-class corvette, nicknamed the 'Zec' by its crews, is a fast and maneuverable escort WarShip built by Illium Naval Engineering at their Illium Yard on Ionus for the Free Worlds League Military. Commissioned in 3058, the Zechetinu was designed to operate as an independent convoy raider, picket ship, or escort vessel, filling a critical gap in the FWLM's naval order of battle that had persisted since the Succession Wars. The class earned a reputation for punching well above its weight, mounting a broadside capability that led many fleet officers to consider it more akin to a destroyer than a true corvette. Its compact hull and exceptional acceleration made it one of the most agile capital vessels of its generation, well suited to the raiding and screening roles the League demanded.</p>",
    "capabilities": "<p>At 180,000 tons and 440 meters, the Zechetinu is one of the smallest WarShips of its era but packs a disproportionate punch. The Block I mounts three NAC/20 naval autocannons across nose and broadside arcs, six NL35 and two NL45 naval lasers in the forward and aft arcs, and two NL55 naval lasers covering the aft quarters. Sixteen ER large lasers provide sustained anti-fighter firepower across all arcs, supported by thirty-two small lasers for point defense. Four LRM 20 launchers with Artemis IV fire control, four SRM 6 launchers with Artemis IV, and eight LB 10-X autocannons round out the conventional armament. The Block II replaces the fore and aft NL35 batteries with White Shark capital missiles and adds Barracuda launchers to the forward and aft quarters, exchanging sustained laser damage for long-range missile striking power. One thousand eight hundred seventy-three double heat sinks manage the enormous thermal load. Ninety tons of lamellor ferro-carbide armor provide relatively light protection, a deliberate tradeoff for the design's exceptional speed. A lithium-fusion battery enables rapid successive jumps. The Block I uniquely carries a mobile HPG, a rare piece of equipment on non-Clan vessels. One docking collar, six aerospace fighters, a single 88-meter gravity deck, and approximately 15,000 tons of cargo complete the design.</p>",
    "deployment": "<p>The FWLS Sparta was one of four Block I Zechetinu corvettes on active service with the FWLM by 3067, alongside the Tirana, Karelia, and Attica. During shakedown trials in early 3059 in the Simpson Desert system, the Sparta experienced structural problems with overstress found on major bulkheads, requiring a return to the shipyard before entering active duty under Captain Roberto Gheorghiu. The Sparta was destroyed or captured at the Battle of Atreus on 25 October 3068, when Blakist-controlled Free Worlds League WarShips turned on loyalist vessels. Of the entire loyalist force, only the FWLS Acari and FWLS Raven escaped to seek refuge in the Duchy of Oriente.</p>",
    "history": "<p>The Zechetinu-class corvette was born from the Free Worlds League's determination to rebuild its naval arm in the wake of the Clan Invasion. Illium Naval Engineering on Ionus received the contract and produced a compact, fast escort design that entered service in 3058. The first vessel's outstanding performance in mock battle exercises led to an expanded production order of ten additional hulls, establishing the Zechetinu as a cornerstone of the FWLM's naval expansion program.</p><p>Production soon shifted to a revised Block II standard that traded the original sustained-fire capital weapons for a missile-oriented armament, providing greater flexibility at extended range. By 3067, four Block I vessels and multiple Block II corvettes were in active service across Free Worlds League space, patrolling trade routes and serving as picket elements for heavier fleet formations. Crew life aboard the Zechetinu was austere even by WarShip standards, with exceedingly cramped quarters necessitating monthly port visits to maintain morale. The vessel's corridors and cargo bays commonly served as exercise areas, supplementing the single small gravity deck. Despite these hardships, the corvette's crews developed a fierce pride in their vessel's speed and firepower, and the 'Zec' earned a loyal following within the FWLM fleet.</p><p>The Jihad proved catastrophic for the class. More than half of all Zechetinus in Free Worlds League service had been secretly infiltrated by Word of Blake personnel, and those vessels promptly defected to the Blakists. The simmering conflict erupted at the Battle of Atreus on 25 October 3068, where a devastating engagement between loyalist and Blakist-aligned League WarShips shattered the loyalist fleet. In the broader Jihad that followed, every remaining Zechetinu was destroyed in combat, seized in internecine fighting between League factions, or lost to the wilds of the Periphery with crews who chose flight over surrender. The class was entirely extinct by the war's end, a cautionary tale of how quickly a promising naval program could be undone by infiltration and civil war.</p>",
    "manufacturer": "Illium Naval Engineering",
    "primaryFactory": "Ionus"
  }
}